<title>GERMANY: Details of German govt annual economic forecast.</title>
<headline>Details of German govt annual economic forecast.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are key forecasts from the German government's annual economic report, details of which were obtained by Reuters on Tuesday. (Figures are real percentage changes unless stated)</p>
<p>					 1997	 1996	  1995</p>
<p> Pan-German GDP		    +2.5	 +1.4	  +1.9</p>
<p> West German GDP		   +2.5	 +1.3	  +1.6</p>
<p> East German GDP		   +2.5	 +2.0	  +5.3</p>
<p> Pan-German unemployment (pct) 11.0	 10.3	   9.4</p>
<p> West German unemployment	 9.5	  9.0	   8.3</p>
<p> East German unemployment	16.0	 15.7	  14.1</p>
<p> Private consumption	     +1.5	 +1.4	  +1.8</p>
<p> State consumption		 +0.5	 +2.8	  +2.0</p>
<p> Industry investment	     +1.5	 -0.7	  +1.5</p>
<p> Exports			     +6.5	 +4.6	  +5.9</p>
<p> Imports			     +4.5	 +2.0	  +6.4</p>
<p> Consumer prices		   +1.5	 +1.8	  +1.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Forecast figures are rounded to the nearest half percentage point. Figures are from a draft annual report to be published by the Economics Ministry on January 28.</p>
<p>--Bonn newsroom +49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
